    <briefdescription>
<para>Threshold-only confidence calibration interface. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Design constraints:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_i_confidence_calibrator_1a7478cd7bf652bb090ba4bdf70b59fddb" kindref="member">calibrate()</ref> operates exclusively on threshold scalars.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>It must never access gradient state, weight tensors, or optimizer state.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_i_confidence_calibrator_1a291e52386d4db87459f0f2ff7d1aab5b" kindref="member">applyThresholds()</ref> updates only the internal threshold store.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_i_confidence_calibrator_1a34c4ac569e6cf0e23d46f1cef8f11c4f" kindref="member">resetToDefaults()</ref> restores factory thresholds without touching any model.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_confidence_calibrator" kindref="compound">ConfidenceCalibrator</ref> (concrete implementation) </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
